gcc 8: do not fold M_PI arithmetic into constexpr under -frounding-math

CGAL forces -frounding-math. With that flag gcc 8 (RHEL 8 / UBI 8) refuses
to evaluate floating-point arithmetic in a constexpr initializer:

  Chamfer.cpp:372:57: error: '(1.5707963267948966e+1 / 1.8e+2)' is not a
  constant expression

gcc 9+ accepts it. These are function-local constants, so `const` gives
the same result on every compiler.

diff --git a/src/algorithm/Chamfer.cpp b/src/algorithm/Chamfer.cpp
index 474bc37..1202dc5 100644
--- a/src/algorithm/Chamfer.cpp
+++ b/src/algorithm/Chamfer.cpp
@@ -369,8 +369,8 @@ create_cutter_for_edge(const Surface_mesh_3 &mesh, const LineString &edge,
   const double opening_angle = M_PI - alpha;
 
   // Validate opening angle range
-  constexpr double MIN_OPENING = MIN_OPENING_DEG * M_PI / 180.0;
-  constexpr double MAX_OPENING = MAX_OPENING_DEG * M_PI / 180.0;
+  const double MIN_OPENING = MIN_OPENING_DEG * M_PI / 180.0;
+  const double MAX_OPENING = MAX_OPENING_DEG * M_PI / 180.0;
 
   if (opening_angle < MIN_OPENING) {
